# G18: keys held down in graphics (dos/tools/keys-x11.sh holds each key for a second or two in a virtual X server; DOSBox's keyboard
# repeats it as a real one does). A toggle acts once however long the key is held; the cursor keys keep repeating. The host plays one press
# of each toggle and enough presses of Left to reach the start, so the frame the program ends on is the same. AUTOTYPE has no Ctrl tokens,
# so this file is played on the host and by the script's own xdotool calls; it is not an e2e.sh scenario.
h i
ctrl-a
ctrl-i          # held: italic once
ctrl-b          # held: bold once
ctrl-u          # held: underline once
right
left left       # held: Left repeats past the start and stops there
ctrl-q          # the question about saving: the frame the script compares
